  "result": "I fixed the four review points in `supported_values_of.rs`, but `./t262 intl402/Intl/supportedValuesOf/` is only 16 of 48 runs passing (the build and clippy are clean).\n\n- **Numbering systems:** the `iter_ids` error is now surfaced as a not-implemented error instead of being dropped. The empty marker attribute now maps to `\"latn\"`. I didn't confirm that the empty attribute is Latin digits in the baked data, so that mapping rests on your review note. I also didn't check that `\"latn\"` appears in the output.\n- **Calendars:** ICU4X documents `HijriSimulatedMecca` and `Julian` as having no CLDR calendar type, so they are skipped. Any other unknown kind now throws not-implemented. I kept the hand-written name table because I found no CLDR-name API in ICU4X.\n- **Time zones:** the code now follows the spec literally. It filters on identifier equal to primary, using the extended parser's normalized and canonical IANA ids, with the Etc/UTC, Etc/GMT and GMT mapping to `UTC`. It skips ICU4X's `Etc/Unknown` placeholder, which is not an IANA id.\n- **Collation, currency, unit:** these stay not-implemented as you said. They account for most of the failures.\n- **Other failures:** several tests also fail because `Intl.DateTimeFormat`, `Intl.Locale`, `Intl.DisplayNames`, `Intl.NumberFormat` and `Intl.RelativeTimeFormat` are not implemented.\n\nBLOCKED: the collation, currency and unit lists need ICU4X data crates that aren't dependencies of `kahvi-builtins`, and Cargo manifests are outside my file scope.",
